WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.525 --> 00:00:17.393
For days the Hwalbindang trained with spears and swords.

2
00:00:19.375 --> 00:00:23.597
Gildong taught them everything he had read about weapons and fighting.

3
00:00:25.778 --> 00:00:28.300
"Robbing the temple was easy," Gildong said.

4
00:00:29.140 --> 00:00:32.161
"Robbing a government storehouse will be much more dangerous."

5
00:00:35.142 --> 00:00:37.902
When he thought they were ready, they went to Hamheung.

6
00:00:41.303 --> 00:00:44.724
Outside the city some of the Hwalbindang gathered straw.

7
00:00:47.025 --> 00:00:50.106
Late that night they went to the old royal villa.

8
00:00:51.286 --> 00:00:53.807
They piled the straw outside the walls.

9
00:00:55.947 --> 00:00:57.728
Gildong took out his fan.

10
00:00:58.556 --> 00:01:02.717
"Fire!" Thwoosh!

11
00:01:03.157 --> 00:01:05.798
The straw lit up in a bright blaze.

12
00:01:11.220 --> 00:01:14.001
The governor in Hamheung was eating a late dinner.

13
00:01:15.561 --> 00:01:18.242
Outside, he heard the city bells ringing.

14
00:01:20.003 --> 00:01:20.703
He sighed.

15
00:01:20.723 --> 00:01:24.544
"I hope it's nothing important."

16
00:01:26.224 --> 00:01:29.427
Just then the captain of the city soldiers arrived.

17
00:01:29.447 --> 00:01:32.790
"Why are you interrupting my meal?"

18
00:01:33.230 --> 00:01:34.311
the governor snapped.

19
00:01:34.331 --> 00:01:39.676
"Sir, there's a fire at the royal villa," the captain said.

20
00:01:39.696 --> 00:01:46.581
"What?" The governor ran outside.

21
00:01:48.403 --> 00:01:50.144
He saw flames in the distance.

22
00:01:50.164 --> 00:01:54.088
"Quick! We must put out the fire!"

23
00:01:54.956 --> 00:01:57.398
"I already sent some soldiers," the captain said.

24
00:01:57.418 --> 00:02:00.000
"Some soldiers?"

25
00:02:00.500 --> 00:02:01.561
the governor cried.

26
00:02:01.581 --> 00:02:03.662
"It's the royal villa!

27
00:02:04.002 --> 00:02:05.764
Send every soldier in the city.

28
00:02:06.504 --> 00:02:08.345
Wake the townspeople too!"

29
00:02:10.367 --> 00:02:13.389
The Hwalbindang were waiting near the government office.

30
00:02:18.712 --> 00:02:21.474
Gildong watched as soldiers ran out the gate.

31
00:02:22.615 --> 00:02:23.496
"Just as I thought!

32
00:02:24.552 --> 00:02:27.513
All the soldiers are leaving to put out the fire," he said.

33
00:02:27.533 --> 00:02:30.814
"No one's guarding the storehouse.

34
00:02:31.294 --> 00:02:31.954
Let's go!"

35
00:02:34.875 --> 00:02:37.836
The thieves made their way into the government office.

36
00:02:40.257 --> 00:02:44.118
They loaded grain and valuables from the storehouse onto carts.

37
00:02:44.138 --> 00:02:48.480
"There's so much here!"

38
00:02:48.980 --> 00:02:49.600
Mok said.

39
00:02:54.572 --> 00:02:57.593
When they finished, Gildong put a sign on the gate.

40
00:02:57.613 --> 00:03:00.735
"What does that say?"

41
00:03:01.235 --> 00:03:02.096
Chibong asked.

42
00:03:02.116 --> 00:03:05.477
"'The Hwalbindang were here,'" Gildong said.

43
00:03:05.497 --> 00:03:08.939
"'This is your punishment for unfair taxes.

44
00:03:09.959 --> 00:03:11.420
Don't mistreat the people again!'"

45
00:03:26.652 --> 00:03:30.556
Lord Hong listened as Police Chief Heup reported to the king.

46
00:03:30.576 --> 00:03:35.340
"Someone started a fire at the royal villa?"

47
00:03:35.780 --> 00:03:36.701
the king cried.

48
00:03:36.721 --> 00:03:39.824
"The government office was robbed too?

49
00:03:40.924 --> 00:03:42.206
Who's responsible?"

50
00:03:42.226 --> 00:03:47.290
"These bandits are the same ones who robbed the temple in Hapcheon.

51
00:03:48.371 --> 00:03:50.152
They call themselves the Hwalbindang.

52
00:03:51.173 --> 00:03:54.056
People say their leader is a boy—Hong Gildong.

53
00:03:57.664 --> 00:03:59.825
He gives the stolen grain to the poor."

54
00:04:03.686 --> 00:04:06.146
boy is causing all this trouble?"

55
00:04:06.526 --> 00:04:07.467
the king cried.

56
00:04:09.227 --> 00:04:10.528
Lord Hong gasped.

57
00:04:10.548 --> 00:04:14.149
"It can't be," he thought.

58
00:04:14.169 --> 00:04:18.770
"Are you all right, minister?"

59
00:04:19.150 --> 00:04:20.010
the king asked.

60
00:04:21.911 --> 00:04:23.671
"I apologize, Your Majesty.

61
00:04:24.691 --> 00:04:27.817
I'm suddenly feeling unwell," Lord Hong said.

62
00:04:27.837 --> 00:04:29.698
"Please excuse me."

63
00:04:31.019 --> 00:04:32.160
Lord Hong bowed.

64
00:04:35.783 --> 00:04:38.525
As he left, he heard the king's command.

65
00:04:38.545 --> 00:04:41.687
"Chief Heup, capture Hong
